&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Urogenital&sol;Anogenital&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; Panels:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;These codes are covered under limited circumstances. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Expanded Respiratory and Pneumonia Panels: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;Covered under limited circumstances. Per policy, these codes are covered in beneficiaries with serious or critical illness or at imminent risk of becoming seriously or critically ill, immunodeficiency, and&sol;or severe underlying condition contributory to testing using an expanded syndromic panel.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Testing is billed according to 1 of the following:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;(a) Places of service (POS) 19, 21, 22, 23, OR&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;(b) The test is ordered as follows (&lt;strong&gt;for healthcare POS other than those listed in (a)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(1) &lt;strong&gt;For immune-competent beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by an Infectious Disease Specialist or Pulmonologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(2)&lt;strong&gt; For immune-compromised beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by a clinician specialist in 1 of the following: Infectious Diseases, Oncology, Transplant (for any panel), or Pulmonologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(3) Regarding (1) and (2), An exception may be made in geographic locations where the specialist(s) cannot be reasonably reached by the beneficiary, and the ordering provider is located closer to the beneficiary&amp;rsquo;s place of residence than the nearest specialist. We would generally expect that beneficiaries for whom the test is ordered under this exception to be living in rural locations, islands, or some other location where access to care is limited.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(4) For testing in POS other than POS 19, 21, 22, or 23, to bill one of the Group 6 CPT codes, &lt;strong&gt;TWO &lt;&sol;strong&gt;ICD-10 codes are required-one from Group 6 and another from Group 1.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expanded Gastrointestinal Panels:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;Covered under limited circumstances. Per policy, these codes are covered in beneficiaries with serious or critical illness or at imminent risk of becoming seriously or critically ill, immunodeficiency, and&sol;or severe underlying condition contributory to testing using an expanded syndromic panel.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Places of service (POS) 19, 21, 22, 23, OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test is ordered as follows (&lt;strong&gt;for healthcare POS other than those listed in (a)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For immune-competent beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by an Infectious Disease Specialist or Gastroenterologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For immune-compromised beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by a clinician specialist in 1 of the following: Infectious Diseases, Oncology, Transplant (for any panel), or Gastroenterologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;Regarding (1) and (2), An exception may be made in geographic locations where the specialist(s) cannot be reasonably reached by the beneficiary, and the ordering provider is located closer to the beneficiary&amp;rsquo;s place of residence than the nearest specialist. We would generally expect that beneficiaries for whom the test is ordered under this exception to be living in rural locations, islands, or some other location where access to care is limited.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;For testing in POS other than POS 19, 21, 22, or 23, to bill one of the Group 7 CPT codes, &lt;strong&gt;TWO &lt;&sol;strong&gt;ICD-10 codes are required-one from Group 7 and another from Group 2.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conditionally Non-covered CPT codes:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The following CPT codes are NOT covered for a given beneficiary on the same DOS when &lt;strong&gt;&amp;gt;1&lt;&sol;strong&gt; is billed in combination with another CPT or PLA code from Groups 1-7 &lt;em&gt;for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Additionally, the following CPT codes are NOT covered for a given beneficiary on the same DOS when &lt;strong&gt;&amp;gt;2&lt;&sol;strong&gt; are billed &lt;em&gt;for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zoonotic Infection Panels:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This code is reimbursed under limited circumstances.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note also the additional diagnostic guidance provided by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC): &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cdc.gov&sol;ticks&sol;hcp&sol;data-research&sol;tickborne-disease-reference-guide&sol;&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;https:&sol;&sol;www.cdc.gov&sol;ticks&sol;hcp&sol;data-research&sol;tickborne-disease-reference-guide&sol;&lt;&sol;a&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CPT codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the laterality of eye procedures, modifiers RT, LT or 50 should be used to indicate the eye(s) being treated.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See L39905 Cataract Surgery LCD and related B&amp;amp;C article for additional coverage indications and diagnoses.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Effective for dates of service 04&sol;01&sol;2024, HCPCS code J0177 should be used to report aflibercept HD for Part A and B services. For services performed 8&sol;18&sol;2023 through 1&sol;1&sol;2024, aflibercept HD should be reported using HCPCS codes J3490, J3590, C9161 or C9399 for Part A and Part B services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Effective for dates of service 10&sol;01&sol;2022, HCPCS code J2777 should be used to report Faricimab-svoa (Vabysmo&amp;#8482;) for Part A and Part B services. Effective for dates of service 07&sol;01&sol;2022 through 09&sol;30&sol;2022, HCPCS code C9097 should be used to report Faricimab-svoa (Vabysmo&amp;#8482;) for Part A services. For dates of service 01&sol;28&sol;2022 through 06&sol;30&sol;2022, HCPCS code J3590 should be used to report Faricimab-svoa (Vabysmo&amp;#8482;) for Part A services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Effective for dates of service 1&sol;28&sol;2022 &lt;&sol;span&gt;through 09&sol;30&sol;2022, &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;HCPCS code J3590 should be used to report Faricimab-svoa (Vabysmo&amp;#8482;) for Part B services.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 04&sol;01&sol;2023, HCPCS code Q5128 should be used to report Ranibizumab-eqrn (CIMERLI&amp;#8482;). Effective for dates of service on or after 08&sol;02&sol;2022 through 03&sol;31&sol;2023, HCPCS codes J3490, J3590 or C9399 should be used to report Ranibizumab-eqrn (CIMERLI&amp;#8482;) for Part A and Part B services.&amp;#160;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Effective for dates of service 4&sol;1&sol;2022 HCPCS code Q5124 should be used to report ranibizumab-nuna, biosimilar, (Byooviz). For dates of service 9&sol;17&sol;2021 through 3&sol;31&sol;2022 HCPCS code J3590 should be used to report ranibizumab-nuna, biosimilar, (Byooviz).&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 10&sol;30&sol;2024 PAVBLU (aflibercept-ayyh) should be reported using HCPCS codes J3490, J3590 for Part B services, or C9399 for Part A services through 3&sol;31&sol;2025. Effective 4&sol;1&sol;2025, PAVBLU (aflibercept-ayyh) should be reported using HCPCS code Q5147.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 4&sol;1&sol;2025,&amp;#160;AHZANTIVE&amp;#174; (aflibercept-mrbb) should be reported using HCPCS code Q5150.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 4&sol;1&sol;2025,&amp;#160;ENZEEVU&amp;#8482; (aflibercept-abzv) should be reported using HCPCS code Q5149.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 7&sol;1&sol;2025, OPUVIZ&amp;#8482;aflibercept-yszy should be reported using HCPCS code Q5153.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 10&sol;1&sol;2025 YESAFILI&amp;#8482;aflibercept-jbvf should be reported using HCPCS code Q5155.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 07&sol;01&sol;2026 Ranibizumab-leyk should be reported using HCPCS code Q5168.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective 07&sol;01&sol;2026 Aflibercept-boav should be reported using HCPCS code Q5170.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For tests billed under the Not Otherwise Classified (NOC) CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; code 81479:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Tests billed under the NOC CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; code 81479 that are used for germline testing and are further defined by a unique identifier (such as a Z-Identifier code) are limited to once per lifetime, as are such tests that are duplicative.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;If non-duplicative testing of such a test is considered medically reasonable and necessary, please use a -77 modifier to trigger a medical review.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For tests billed under the Not Otherwise Classified (NOC) CPT&amp;reg; code 81479:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tests billed under the NOC CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; code 81479 that are used for germline testing and are further defined by a unique identifier (such as a Z-Identifier code) are limited to once per lifetime, as are such tests that are duplicative.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If non-duplicative testing of such a test is considered medically reasonable and necessary, please use a -77 modifier to trigger a medical review.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For tests billed under the Not Otherwise Classified (NOC) CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; code 81479:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Tests billed under the NOC CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; code 81479 that are used for germline testing and are further defined by a unique identifier (such as a Z-Identifier code) are limited to once per lifetime, as are such tests that are duplicative.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;If non-duplicative testing of such a test is considered medically reasonable and necessary, please use a -77 modifier to trigger a medical review.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

