&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tier 2 CPT and NOC Codes&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Refer to indications and Limitations of Coverage section (L35000).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tier 2&sol;NOC Covered Code&sol;Gene Combinations&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Limited coverage may be provided for specific genes reported below:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81400&lt;&sol;strong&gt; ACE, F13B, F5, F7, FGB&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81401&lt;&sol;strong&gt; CBFB-MYH11, E2A&sol;PBX1, EML4-ALK, ETV6-RUNX1, EWSR1&sol;ERG, EWSR1&sol;FLI1, EWSR1&sol;WT1, F11coagulation factor XI, FIP1L1-PDGFR, FOXO1&sol;PAX3, FOXO1&sol;PAX7, MUTYH (mutY homolog [E.coli]), NPM&sol;ALK, PAX8&sol;PPARG, RUNX1&sol;RUNX1T1&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81403&lt;&sol;strong&gt; F8 (coagulation factor VIII), VHL (von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppressor)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81404&lt;&sol;strong&gt; CDKN2A (cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 2A), PRSS1 (protease, serine, 1 [trypsin 1]), MEN1 (multiple endocrine neoplasia 1) (eg, multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1, Wermer syndrome), duplication&sol;deletion, TP53 (tumor protein 53) (e.g. tumor samples), targeted sequence analysis of 2-5 exons, VHL (von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppressor)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81405&lt;&sol;strong&gt; TP53 (tumor protein 53) (e.g. Li-Fraumeni syndrome, tumor samples), full gene sequence or targeted sequence analysis of &amp;gt;5 exons,&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81406&lt;&sol;strong&gt; ATP7B (ATPase, Cu++ transporting, beta polypeptide)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tier 2&sol;NOC Individual Review Code&sol;Gene Combinations&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Any genetic test reported with a Tier 2 CPT code, not listed above or below, is subject to individual review.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tier 2&sol;NOC Non-covered Code&sol;Gene Combinations&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The following individual Tier 2 genetic tests are unlikely to impact therapeutic decision-making, directly impact treatment, outcome and&sol;or clinical management in the care of the beneficiary and will be denied as not medically necessary (Please note that this list of non-covered genes is not exhaustive, and the fact that a specific gene is not mentioned does not mean it is covered. In addition, many genes have several names that are used. The most common names have been used in this article):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81400 &lt;&sol;strong&gt;ABCC8, ACADM, AGTR1, CCR5, CLRN1, DYT1 (TOR1A), FGFR3, IL28B, IVD, TOR1A&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81401&lt;&sol;strong&gt; ADRB2, ATN1, CFH&sol;ARMS2, DEK&sol;NUP214, FGFR3, GALT (galactose-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase), H19, KCNQ10T1 (KCNQ1 overlapping transcript 1), MEG3&sol;DLK1, MLL&sol;AFF, MT-ATP6, MT-ND4, MT-ND6, MT-ND5 mitochondrially encoded tRNA leucine 1 [UUA&sol;G] mitochondrially encoded NADH dehydrogenase 5), MT-RNR1 (mitochondrially encoded 12S RNA), MT-TK (mitochondrially encoded tRNA lysine), MT-TL1, MT-TS1, PRSS1 (protease, serine, 1 [trypsin 1])&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81402&lt;&sol;strong&gt; CYP21A2, Chromosome 18q-, MEFV (Mediterranean fever) (eg, familial Mediterranean fever), TRD 81402 Uniparental disomy (UPD)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81403&lt;&sol;strong&gt; ANG (angiogenin, ribonuclease, RNase A family, 5), FGFR3 (fibroblast growth factor receptor 3) one exon, GJB1 (gap junction protein, beta 1) (eg, Charcot-Marie-Tooth X-linked), full gene sequence, HRAS (v-Ha-ras Harvey rat sarcoma viral oncogene homolog Costello syndrome), MT-RNR1 (mitochondrially encoded 12S RNA), MT-TS1 (mitochondrially encoded tRNA serine 1)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81404&lt;&sol;strong&gt; ACADS (acyl-CoA dehydrogenase), AQP2 (aquaporin 2 [collecting duct]), ARX (aristaless related homeobox), BTD (biotinidase), CAV3 (caveolin 3) (eg, CAV3-related distal myopathy, limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1C), full gene sequence, CLRN1 (clarin 1), CYP1B1 (cytochrome P450, family 1, subfamily B, polypeptide 1), EGR2 (early growth response 2) (eg, Charcot-Marie-Tooth), FGFR2 (fibroblast growth factor receptor 2) (2 EXONS), FGFR3 (fibroblast growth factor receptor 3) (4 EXONS), FKRP (Fukutin related protein), FOXG1 (forkhead box G1), FSHMD1A (facioscapulohumeral muscular dystrophy 1A), FSHMD1A (facioscapulohumeral muscular dystrophy 1A), HNF1B (HNF1 homeobox B), HRAS (v-Ha-ras Harvey rat sarcoma viral oncogene homolog), KCNJ10 (potassium inwardly-rectifying channel, subfamily J, member 10), SLC25A4 (solute carrier family 25 [mitochondrial carrier; adenine nucleotide translocation], VWF (von Willebrand factor)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81405&lt;&sol;strong&gt; CASR (CAR, EIG8, extracellular calcium-sensing receptor, FHH, FIH, GPRC2A, HHC, HHC1, NSHPT, PCAR1), CYP21A2 (cytochrome P450, family 21, subfamily A, polypeptide2), MPZ (myelin protein zero)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81406&lt;&sol;strong&gt; ACADVL (acyl-CoA dehydrogenase, very long chain), CBS (cystathionine-beta-synthase), CDKL5 (cyclin-dependent kinase-like 5) DLAT (dihydrolipoamide S-acetyltransferase), DLD (dihydrolipoamide dehydrogenase), F8 (coagulation factor VIII), GALT (galactose-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase), HADHA (hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase&sol;3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase&sol;enoyl-CoA hydratase [trifunctional protein] alpha subunit), HEXA (hexosaminidase A, alpha polypeptide), LMNA (lamin A&sol;C), MUTYH (mutY homolog [E. coli]), NF2 (neurofibromin 2 [merlin]), NSD1 (nuclear receptor binding SET domain protein 1), PAH (phenylalanine hydroxylase), PAX2 (paired box 2), PDHA1 (pyruvate dehydrogenase [lipoamide] alpha1), POLG (polymerase [DNA directed], gamma), PRKAG2 (protein kinase, AMP-activated, gamma 2 non-catalytic subunit), PTPN11 (protein tyrosine phosphatase, non-receptor type 11), RET (ret-proto-oncogene) (eg, Hirschsprung disease), full gene sequence, SLC9A6 (solute carrier family 9 [sodium&sol;hydrogen exchanger] member 6), SOS1 (son of sevenless homolog 1), TAZ (tafazzin), TSC1 (tuberous sclerosis 1), TSC2 (tuberous sclerosis 2), UBE3A (ubiquitin protein ligase)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81407&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Level 8 Molecular Pathology Procedures, F8 (coagulation factor VIII)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81408&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Level 9 Molecular Pathology Procedures&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;81479&lt;&sol;strong&gt; PIK3C, PI3Ks, PI(3)Ks, PI-3Ks, AKT1, MEK1, VEGFR2 (CD309, FLK1, VEGFR), LPA intron 25 genotype, KIF6, SPG4, C9orf72, MLH1, AIRE (APSI), SDA2, HAX1 (HAX1_HUMAN, HCLS1- associated protein X-1, HCLSBP1, HS1-associating protein X-1, HS1 binding protein, HS1-binding protein 1, HS1BP1, HSP1BP-1)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; When a panel with greater than one or less than five genes is ordered, use the corresponding existing panel CPT code or CPT code 81479 if none exists.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.65pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;The CPT codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the laterality of eye procedures, modifiers RT, LT or 50 must be used to indicate the eye(s) being treated.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See L33558 Cataract Extraction LCD and related Billing and Coding article for additional coverage indications and diagnoses.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Below are CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&sol;HCPCS codes related to SRT.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in their CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; books.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per CPT 2026 guidance SRT should not be reported in conjunction with megavoltage (MeV) (77402, 77407, 77412).&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; To bill electronic brachytherapy treatment delivery use CPT code 77437 (e.g., electronic brachytherapy). When billing 77437 for SRT treatment delivery services covered by the LCD providers must append the KX modifier. &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For SRT treatment planning and simulation aided field setting use CPT code 77436.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CPT 77436 is not typically repeated with each treatment except when clinically indicated and documentation supports additional simulation requirements. Do not report clinical treatment planning (77261, 77262, 77263), simulation (77280, 77285, 77290, 77295), basic dosimetry calculation (77300), special dosimetry (77331), treatment devices (77332, 77333, 77334), isodose planning (77306, 77307, 77316, 77317, 77318), or radiation treatment management (77427, 77431, 77432, 77435, 77469, 77470, 77499) in conjunction with 77436 and 77437.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code 77336 can only be billed when medically necessary for treatment adjustments in support of the radiation oncologist or other health care qualified professional.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code 77370 is to be used when the complexity of the treatment plan is great. It is not expected that code 77370 will be reported for SRT services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use of 77370 with SRT code 77437 may lead to medical review.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This list represents common physical and occupational therapy services and is not all-inclusive.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HCPCS code G0295 is status N (non-covered) under Medicare.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CPT code 97037 is status N (non-covered) under Medicare.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Effective for dates of service on or after 04&sol;01&sol;2021, HCPCS code J7321 should be used to report Visco-3&amp;trade;.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Report&amp;nbsp;HCPCS code C9465 for&amp;nbsp;Durolane&amp;reg; when billed to the Part A MAC and HCPCS code J3490&amp;nbsp;when billed to the Part B MAC for dates of service prior to 01&sol;01&sol;2019.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For dates of service on or after 10&sol;01&sol;2019 HCPCS code J7331 should be used to report Synojoynt&amp;trade;.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For dates of service on or after 10&sol;01&sol;2019 HCPCS code J7332 should be used to report Triluron&amp;trade;.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
