&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Effective for dates of service on or after 01&sol;01&sol;2023, leuprolide acetate for depot suspension (Lutrate) should be reported with HCPCS code J1954.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Effective for dates of service on or after 01&sol;01&sol;2022, leuprolide mesylate (Camcevi&amp;reg;), should be reported with HCPCS code J1952.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective for dates of service 5&sol;26&sol;2021 through 12&sol;31&sol;2021, leuprolide mesylate (Camcevi&amp;reg;), should be reported with HCPCS code J3590.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CPT Code J9218 is not covered under Medicare because it is self-administered.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly Multiplexed GPPs- Group 2 Codes&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Must be billed in POS 20, 21, 22, 23, or 81 (Urgent Care, Inpatient Hospital, Outpatient Hospital (observation), or Emergency Room), or in POS 81 (Independent Laboratory) in the case of a pre-transplant evaluation for an immune-compromised beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Outside of one of these POS, a clinician specialist in one of the following: Infectious Diseases (44), Gastroenterology (10), Oncology (83,90,91), or Transplant&amp;nbsp;must either order the test or communicate with the treating and ordering physician as to appropriate test and interpretation.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The specialist communication must be documented in the medical record.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;CPT code 0097U was deleted. effective for services rendered on or after 4&sol;1&sol;2022.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;HCPCS code J1300 should be used to report eculizumab, effective 01&sol;01&sol;2025 through 03&sol;31&sol;2025.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HCPCS code J1300 has been deleted and replaced by HCPCS codes J1299, effective 4&sol;1&sol;2025.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HCPCS code Q5139 should be used to report eculizumab-aeeb, effective 01&sol;01&sol;2025 through 03&sol;31&sol;2025.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HCPCS code Q5139 has been deleted and replaced by HCPCS codes Q5152, and should be used to report eculizumab-aeeb, effective 4&sol;1&sol;2025.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HCPCS code Q5151 has been added and should be used to report eculixumab-aagh, effective 4&sol;1&sol;2025.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective for dates of service on or after 05&sol;01&sol;2021, the administration of eculizumab should be billed using the intravenous infusion administration codes (Refer to article A58620 - Billing and Coding: Complex Drug Administration Coding).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For dates of service prior to 05&sol;01&sol;2021, administration of eculizumab may be billed using the chemotherapy administration code 96413 - Chemotherapy administration, intravenous infusion technique; up to 1 hour, single or initial substance&sol;drug and 96415 - Chemotherapy administration, intravenous infusion technique; each additional hour (List separately in addition to code for primary procedure) when required due to infusion related adverse reactions in adults (up to 2 hours total) or when used in pediatric or aged Medicare beneficiaries (up to 4 hours total).&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following CPT&sol;HCPCS codes are non-covered*:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* this is not an inclusive list of non-covered codes&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Note: 64492 or 64495 describes a third and additional levels and should be listed separately in addition to the code for the primary procedure and the second level procedure and cannot be reported more than once per day. 64492 should be reported in conjunction with 64490&sol;64491 and 64495 should be reported in conjunction with 64493&sol;64494. Codes 64492 and 64495 will only be covered upon appeal if sufficient documentation of medical necessity is present.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The CPT codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when ordered by a physician or other qualified health care professional (i.e., NP, CNS, PA).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4K Score &lt;&sol;strong&gt;should be billed with 81539&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PCA3 &lt;&sol;strong&gt;should be billed using code 81313&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ConfirmDx &lt;&sol;strong&gt;should be billed using code 81551&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;%fPSA &lt;&sol;strong&gt;should be billed using codes 84153 and 84154.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHI &lt;&sol;strong&gt;should be billed using codes 84153, 84154 and 86316.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SelectMDX&lt;&sol;strong&gt; should be billed using code 81479&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;EPI&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt; should be billed using code 0005U.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Procedure codes may be subject to National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits or OPPS packaging edits. Refer to NCCI and OPPS requirements prior to billing Medicare.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For services requiring a referring&sol;ordering physician, the name and NPI of the referring&sol;ordering physician must be reported on the claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A claim submitted without a valid ICD-10-CM diagnosis code will be returned to the provider as an incomplete claim under &amp;sect;1833(e) of the Social Security Act.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;All services&sol;procedures performed on the same day for the same beneficiary by the physician&sol;provider should be billed on the same claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Billing for preparatory services&sol;acquisition costs is covered in CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 3, &amp;sect;90.3.1 Allogeneic for Stem Cell Transplantation.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

