&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in their CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; book.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;The CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when the &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Indications of Coverage &lt;&sol;span&gt;are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Due to the laterality of eye procedures, modifiers RT, LT or 50 should be used to indicate the eye(s) being treated.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;See &lt;strong&gt;Cataract Surgery L34413 LCD&lt;&sol;strong&gt; and related &lt;strong&gt;Billing and Coding: Cataract Surgery A56613 Article&lt;&sol;strong&gt; for additional coverage indications and diagnoses.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;The CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in Group 2: Codes are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Do not report 0671T in conjunction with 66989 or 66991.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CPT codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Due to the laterality of eye procedures, modifiers RT, LT or 50 must be used to indicate the eye(s) being treated.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See L34203 Cataract Surgery in Adults LCD and related B&amp;amp;C article for additional coverage indications and diagnoses.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

