&lt;p&gt;Below are CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&sol;HCPCS codes related to SRT.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in their CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; books.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per CPT 2026 guidance SRT should not be reported in conjunction with megavoltage (MeV) (77402, 77407, 77412).&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; To bill electronic brachytherapy treatment delivery use CPT code 77437 (e.g., electronic brachytherapy). When billing 77437 for SRT treatment delivery services covered by the LCD providers must append the KX modifier. &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For SRT treatment planning and simulation aided field setting use CPT code 77436.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CPT 77436 is not typically repeated with each treatment except when clinically indicated and documentation supports additional simulation requirements. Do not report clinical treatment planning (77261, 77262, 77263), simulation (77280, 77285, 77290, 77295), basic dosimetry calculation (77300), special dosimetry (77331), treatment devices (77332, 77333, 77334), isodose planning (77306, 77307, 77316, 77317, 77318), or radiation treatment management (77427, 77431, 77432, 77435, 77469, 77470, 77499) in conjunction with 77436 and 77437.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code 77336 can only be billed when medically necessary for treatment adjustments in support of the radiation oncologist or other health care qualified professional.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code 77370 is to be used when the complexity of the treatment plan is great. It is not expected that code 77370 will be reported for SRT services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use of 77370 with SRT code 77437 may lead to medical review.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Below are CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&sol;HCPCS codes related to SRT.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in their CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; books&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Per CPT 2026 guidance SRT should not be reported in conjunction with megavoltage (MeV) (77402, 77407, 77412). To bill electronic brachytherapy treatment delivery use CPT code 77437 (e.g., electronic brachytherapy). When billing 77437 for SRT treatment delivery services covered by the LCD providers must append the KX modifier. For SRT treatment planning and simulation aided field setting use CPT code 77436. CPT 77436 is not typically repeated with each treatment except when clinically indicated and documentation supports additional simulation requirements. Do not report clinical treatment planning (77261, 77262, 77263), simulation (77280, 77285, 77290, 77295), basic dosimetry calculation (77300), special dosimetry (77331), treatment devices (77332, 77333, 77334), isodose planning (77306, 77307, 77316, 77317, 77318), or radiation treatment management (77427, 77431, 77432, 77435, 77469, 77470, 77499) in conjunction with 77436 and 77437.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code 77336 can only be billed when medically necessary for treatment adjustments in support of the radiation oncologist or other health care qualified professional.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code 77370 is to be used when the complexity of the treatment plan is great. It is not expected that code 77370 will be reported for SRT services. Use of 77370 with SRT code 77437 may lead to medical review.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Below are CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&sol;HCPCS codes related to SRT.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes in their CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; books.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per CPT&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 2026 guidance, SRT should not be reported in conjunction with megavoltage (MeV) (77402, 77407, 77412).&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To bill electronic brachytherapy (EBT) treatment delivery use CPT&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;strong&gt; code 77437 (e.g., electronic brachytherapy). When billing 77437 for SRT treatment delivery services covered by the LCD providers must append the KX modifier.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For SRT treatment planning and simulation aided field setting use CPT&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;strong&gt; code 77436.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; 77436 is not typically repeated with each treatment except when clinically indicated and documentation supports additional simulation requirements. Do not report clinical treatment planning (77261, 77262, 77263), simulation (77280, 77285, 77290, 77295), basic dosimetry calculation (77300), special dosimetry (77331), treatment devices (77332, 77333, 77334), isodose planning (77306, 77307, 77316, 77317, 77318), or radiation treatment management (77427, 77431, 77432, 77435, 77469, 77470, 77499) in conjunction with 77436 and 77437.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;Code 77336 can only be billed when medically necessary for treatment adjustments in support of the radiation oncologist or other health care qualified professional.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;Code 77370 is to be used when the complexity of the treatment plan is great. It is not expected that CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;code 77370 will be reported for SRT services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Use of 77370 with SRT code 77437 may lead to medical review.&lt;&sol;p&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Procedure codes may be subject to National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits or OPPS packaging edits. Refer to NCCI and OPPS requirements prior to billing Medicare.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For services requiring a referring&sol;ordering physician, the name and NPI of the referring&sol;ordering physician must be reported on the claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A claim submitted without a valid ICD-10-CM diagnosis code will be returned to the provider as an incomplete claim under &amp;sect;1833(e) of the Social Security Act.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;All services&sol;procedures performed on the same day for the same beneficiary by the physician&sol;provider should be billed on the same claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Billing for preparatory services&sol;acquisition costs is covered in CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 3, &amp;sect;90.3.1 Allogeneic for Stem Cell Transplantation.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2 Codes covered by the provisions of this Local Coverage Determination.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT Code Book)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The addition of the level of treatment should be recorded with any other modifier required on the claim line with the procedure code.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 13.95pt;&quot;&gt;Procedure codes may be subject to National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits or OPPS packaging edits. Refer to NCCI and OPPS requirements prior to billing Medicare.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 13.9pt;&quot;&gt;For services requiring a referring&sol;ordering physician, the name and NPI of the referring&sol;ordering physician must be reported on the claim.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 13.9pt;&quot;&gt;A claim submitted without a valid ICD-10-CM diagnosis code will be returned to the provider as an incomplete claim under &amp;sect;1833(e) of the Social Security Act.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 13.9pt;&quot;&gt;All services&sol;procedures performed on the same day for the same beneficiary by the physician&sol;provider should be billed on the same claim.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 13.95pt;&quot;&gt;Billing for preparatory services is covered in CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 3, &amp;sect;90.3.1 Allogeneic for Stem Cell Transplantation.&lt;&sol;p&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

