&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Urogenital&sol;Anogenital&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; Panels:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;These codes are covered under limited circumstances.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Expanded Respiratory and Pneumonia Panels: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Covered under limited circumstances. Per policy, these codes are covered in beneficiaries with serious or critical illness or at imminent risk of becoming seriously or critically ill, immunodeficiency, and&sol;or severe underlying condition contributory to testing using an expanded syndromic panel. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Testing is billed according to 1 of the following:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;(a) Places of service (POS) 19, 21, 22, 23, OR&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;(b) The test is ordered as follows (&lt;strong&gt;for healthcare POS other than those listed in (a)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(1) &lt;strong&gt;For immune-competent beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by an Infectious Disease Specialist or Pulmonologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(2)&lt;strong&gt; For immune-compromised beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by a clinician specialist in 1 of the following: Infectious Diseases, Oncology, Transplant (for any panel), or Pulmonologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(3) Regarding (1) and (2), An exception may be made in geographic locations where the specialist(s) cannot be reasonably reached by the beneficiary, and the ordering provider is located closer to the beneficiary&amp;rsquo;s place of residence than the nearest specialist. We would generally expect that beneficiaries for whom the test is ordered under this exception to be living in rural locations, islands, or some other location where access to care is limited.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 120px;&quot;&gt;(4) For testing in POS other than POS 19, 21, 22, or 23, to bill one of the Group 6 CPT codes, &lt;strong&gt;TWO &lt;&sol;strong&gt;ICD-10 codes are required-one from Group 6 and another from Group 1.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Expanded Gastrointestinal Panels:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Covered under limited circumstances. Per policy, these codes are covered in beneficiaries with serious or critical illness or at imminent risk of becoming seriously or critically ill, immunodeficiency, and&sol;or severe underlying condition contributory to testing using an expanded syndromic panel. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;(a) Places of service (POS) 19, 21, 22, 23, OR&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;(b) The test is ordered as follows (&lt;strong&gt;for healthcare POS other than those listed in (a)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;(1) &lt;strong&gt;For immune-competent beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by an Infectious Disease Specialist or Gastroenterologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%; padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;(2)&lt;strong&gt; For immune-compromised beneficiaries&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, the test must be ordered by a clinician specialist in 1 of the following: Infectious Diseases, Oncology, Transplant (for any panel), or Gastroenterologist who is diagnosing and treating the beneficiary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;(3) Regarding (1) and (2), An exception may be made in geographic locations where the specialist(s) cannot be reasonably reached by the beneficiary, and the ordering provider is located closer to the beneficiary&amp;rsquo;s place of residence than the nearest specialist. We would generally expect that beneficiaries for whom the test is ordered under this exception to be living in rural locations, islands, or some other location where access to care is limited.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;(4) For testing in POS other than POS 19, 21, 22, or 23, to bill one of the Group 7 CPT codes, &lt;strong&gt;TWO &lt;&sol;strong&gt;ICD-10 codes are required-one from Group 7 and another from Group 2.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conditionally Non-covered CPT codes:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The following CPT codes are NOT covered for a given beneficiary on the same DOS when &lt;strong&gt;&amp;gt;1&lt;&sol;strong&gt; is billed in combination with another CPT or PLA code from Groups 1-7 &lt;em&gt;for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Additionally, the following CPT codes are NOT covered for a given beneficiary on the same DOS when &lt;strong&gt;&amp;gt;2&lt;&sol;strong&gt; are billed &lt;em&gt;for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

