&lt;p&gt;The addition of the level of treatment should be recorded with any other modifier required on the claim line with the procedure code.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Procedure codes may be subject to National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits or OPPS packaging edits. Refer to NCCI and OPPS requirements prior to billing Medicare.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For services requiring a referring&sol;ordering physician, the name and NPI of the referring&sol;ordering physician must be reported on the claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A claim submitted without a valid ICD-10-CM diagnosis code will be returned to the provider as an incomplete claim under &amp;sect;1833(e) of the Social Security Act.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;All services&sol;procedures performed on the same day for the same beneficiary by the physician&sol;provider should be billed on the same claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Billing for preparatory services&sol;acquisition costs is covered in CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 3, &amp;sect;90.3.1 Allogeneic for Stem Cell Transplantation.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Injection of a chemodenervation agent for the treatment of achalasia is a procedure that should be done by providers with training to treat diseases of the gastrointestinal (GI) tract (e.g., gastroenterologists and surgeons). Refer to the Upper Gastrointestinal Endoscopy and Visualization L34434 LCD for guidelines for the treatment of achalasia.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes 95873 and 95874, in addition to, the code for the primary procedure CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes 64612, 64615, 64616, 64642, 64643, 64644, 64645, 64646, 64647, 64653, 64999.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;!&amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;StartFragment &amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pf0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf0&quot;&gt;The following should be reported for ABL1 Kinase Domain Mutation Analysis for the detection of acquired imatinib tyrosine kinase inhibitor resistance.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
