&lt;p class=&quot;pf0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf0&quot;&gt;These code(s) are non-covered.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;!&amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;EndFragment &amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CLONOSEQ&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;81479 for claims on or after 3&sol;16&sol;2018&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use PLA 0364U to describe the service for patients with a personal history of cancer. This code has been approved for patients with a history of Mantle Cell Lymphoma.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-gene and panel testing by PCR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding single-gene and panel testing of genes &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A57527 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A58121&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding BCR-ABL1 testing &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A55600 for BCR-ABL1 testing&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Code 90863 is to be coded with 90832, 90834, 90837.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Codes 90833,90836, 90838 are to be coded with 99202-99255, 99304-99306, 99341-99350.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Code 90840, code first 90839.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;90785, code first 90791-90792, 90832-90834, 90836-90838, 90853.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;90785 excludes 97151, 97152, 97153, 97154, 97155, 97156, 97157, 97158, 0362T, 0373T, 90839,90840, 96136-96139, 96146, 96130-96133.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facial and Maxillofacial Procedures&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;codes only when the physician actually designs and prepares the prosthesis and not when the prosthesis is prepared by an outside laboratory.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; codes 21089 and 21299 are billed, documentation must be submitted with the claim.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CLONOSEQ&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;81479 for claims on or after 3&sol;16&sol;2018&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use PLA 0364U to describe the service for patients with a personal history of cancer. This code has been approved for patients with a history of Mantle Cell Lymphoma.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-gene and panel testing by PCR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding single-gene and panel testing of genes &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A57526 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A58120&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding BCR-ABL1 testing &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A55595 for BCR-ABL1 testing&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following tests may be billed in the post-biopsy setting (after a negative or non-malignant biopsy, as defined in the policy) for individuals contemplating a repeat biopsy:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progensa PCA3 assay (CPT 81313), performed on post-digital rectal exam (DRE) urine specimens&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ConfirmMDx assay (CPT 81551), performed on formalin-fixed, paraffin embedded (FFPE) tissue specimens.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MyProstate Score 2.0 (MPS 2.0) (PLA 0403U), performed on first catch urine specimens&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following test may be billed in the pre-biopsy setting as defined in the policy:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SelectMDx assay (PLA 0339U), performed on post-digital rectal exam (DRE) urine specimens&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MyProstate Score 2.0 (MPS 2.0) (PLA 0403U), performed on first catch urine specimens&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Primary codes: G2067-G2075&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Do not report more than 1 primary code per 7-day period.&lt;&sol;span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;If a patient switches from one medication to another, bill for one code describing a weekly bundled payment for that week and use the code for the medication given for most of the week.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G2069 and G2073 may be reported only once in a 4-week period&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G2070 and G2072 may be reported only once in a 6-month period&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Add on codes: G0137, G1028, G2076-G2080, G2215-2216&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G2076 should be reported for intake activities of new patients and include and initial assessment as outline in the LCD. A new patient is one who has not been seen for OTP care within the last 12 months.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G2078 and G2079 may be reported up to 3 times in a 1-month period. These are used in addition to the weekly bundled payment code. Do not bill for take-home supplies of medication for dates of service that overlap with the weekly bundled payment codes describing a medication bundle (G2067-G2073).&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G2080 may be reported only when medically reasonable and necessary counseling or therapy services largely exceed the amount listed in the patient&amp;rsquo;s individualized treatment plan.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G2215, G2216, and G1028 may be reported only once every 30 days unless an additional take-home supply of the medication is medically reasonable and necessary. This should be clearly documented.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;G0137 may be reported if the patient receives at least 9 intensive outpatient (IOP) services in a week&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;- Use only if the patient has a need for a minimum of 9 hours of IOP services a week&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;- Use only if the patient requires a higher level of care intensity compared to other non-intensive outpatient OTP services&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following CPT&sol;HCPCS codes are covered additional services considered necessary to perform diagnostic testing in an IDTF.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Positron emission tomography (PET) Radiopharmaceutical&sol;Tracer codes A9597 or A9598 should only be used when there is no existing dedicated PET tracer code available (reference &lt;em&gt;Medicare Claims Processing Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, Chapter 13, Section 60.3.2). For additional information, please refer to A53134 NCD Coding Article for Positron Emission Tomography (PET) Scans Used for Non-Oncologic Conditions.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Effective for claims with dates of service on or after 12&sol;15&sol;2017, HCPCS code A9580 (NaF-18) is nationally non-covered and all associated NaF-18 PET related coding including PET scan CPT codes are also non-covered.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following CPT&sol;HCPCS codes are covered additional services considered necessary to perform diagnostic testing in an IDTF.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Positron emission tomography (PET) Radiopharmaceutical&sol;Tracer codes A9597 or A9598 should only be used when there is no existing dedicated PET tracer code available (reference &lt;em&gt;Medicare Claims Processing Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, Chapter 13, Section 60.3.2). For additional information, please refer to A53134 NCD Coding Article for Positron Emission Tomography (PET) Scans Used for Non-Oncologic Conditions.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Effective for claims with dates of service on or after 12&sol;15&sol;2017, HCPCS code A9580 (NaF-18) is nationally non-covered and all associated NaF-18 PET related coding including PET scan CPT codes are also non-covered.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CPT codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See L37027 Cataract Surgery in Adults LCD and related B&amp;amp;C article for additional coverage indications and diagnoses.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Angiography&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the arteries in the &lt;strong&gt;Abdomen, Pelvis, &lt;&sol;strong&gt;or&lt;strong&gt; Lower Extremity&lt;&sol;strong&gt; branches. &lt;strong&gt;Aortography&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the arteries in the &lt;strong&gt;Abdomen&lt;&sol;strong&gt; with or without the &lt;strong&gt;Lower Extremity&lt;&sol;strong&gt; arteries.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&sol;HCPCS codes in their CPT&sol;HCPCS book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following CPT code associated with the services outlined in this Billing and Coding Article will not have diagnosis code limitations applied at this time: &lt;strong&gt;36200&lt;&sol;strong&gt;.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Angiography&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the arteries in the &lt;strong&gt;Abdomen, Pelvis, &lt;&sol;strong&gt;or&lt;strong&gt; Lower Extremity&lt;&sol;strong&gt; branches. &lt;strong&gt;Aortography&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the arteries in the &lt;strong&gt;Abdomen&lt;&sol;strong&gt; with or without the &lt;strong&gt;Lower Extremity&lt;&sol;strong&gt; arteries.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;&sol;strong&gt;: Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT&sol;HCPCS codes in their CPT&sol;HCPCS book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following CPT code associated with the services outlined in this Billing and Coding Article will not have diagnosis limitations applied at this time:&lt;strong&gt; 36200.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; The following CPT codes associated with the services outlined in this Billing and Coding Article will not have diagnosis code limitations applied at this time: &lt;strong&gt;82180, 84252, 84425, 84446, 84590, and 84597.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code 82306 includes fractions, if performed. &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code 82652 includes fractions, if performed.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To bill for this service, enter 64999 in the comment field as listed below with the description SphenoCath&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; or the name of the delivery device used.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Part A:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2300 loop, NTE segment for the electronic claim&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Form Locator 80 Remarks on the UB04 form&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Part B:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loop 2400&sol;SV101-7 for the electronic claim or&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Item 19 on the CMS-1500 paper claim form&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;;&quot;&gt;Do not use &lt;&sol;span&gt;CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;64400 and&sol;or 64505 to bill for this device.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
