&lt;p&gt;To bill for this service, enter 64999 in the comment field as listed below with the description SphenoCath&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;or the name of the delivery device used.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Part A:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2300 loop. NTE segment for the electronic claim&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Form Locator 80 Remarks on the UB04 form&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Part B:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loop 2400&sol;SV101-7 for the electronic claim or&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Item 19 on the CMS-1500 paper claim form&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;;&quot;&gt;Do not use &lt;&sol;span&gt;CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;64400 and&sol;or 64505 to bill for this device.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use J7999-KD* to indicate compounded and&sol;or combination drugs used in implantable infusion pumps including, morphine sulfate, hydromorphone, fentanyl, sufentanil, clonidine, bupivacaine, compounded baclofen, and ziconitide. Other drugs are not covered. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;When non-compounded or single agent drugs are used in implantable infusion pumps, use the specific HCPCS code for the drug used. Only the following non-compounded drugs are covered: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;J2278-KD ziconitide (Prialt&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) (non-compounded) (For &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ICD-10-CM Codes that Support Medical Necessity Group 3: Codes&lt;&sol;em&gt; only&lt;&sol;strong&gt;) &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;J0475-KD Injection, baclofen &lt;strong&gt;(non-compounded)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;, 10 mg &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;J9200-KD floxuridine (non-compounded) (For &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ICD-10-CM Codes that Support Medical Necessity Group 1: Codes&lt;&sol;em&gt; only&lt;&sol;strong&gt;) &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*CPT&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; codes 62322, 62323, 62326 and 62327 should be reported when performing trial infusions prior to permanent pump implantation. Choose the appropriate code as to whether the trial involves intermittent boluses or continuous infusion i.e., baclofen trials, without placement of a catheter or with placement of a catheter that will remain in place less than 24 hours (62322, 62323); or a trial that involves intermittent boluses or continuous infusion through a catheter that will remain in place greater than 24 hours (62326, 62327).&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;&sol;strong&gt;: Please see the indications and limitations section of the LCD for details regarding CPT&sol;HCPCS codes: 81292, 81293, 81294, 81321, 81322, 81323, 81437, 81479, 81520, 81525, 81540, and 81546.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see NCD 90.2, Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) for Patients with Advanced Cancer.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-gene and panel testing by PCR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regarding single-gene and panel testing of genes &amp;ndash; Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A57772 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A57880&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regarding BCR-ABL1 testing &amp;ndash; Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A55233 for BCR-ABL1 testing&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CLONOSEQ&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;81479 for claims on or after 3&sol;16&sol;2018&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use PLA 0364U to describe the service for patients with a personal history of cancer. This code has been approved for patients with a history of Mantle Cell Lymphoma.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-gene and panel testing by PCR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding single-gene and panel testing of genes &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A56853 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A57503&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding BCR-ABL1 testing &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A53531 for BCR-ABL1 testing&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CLONOSEQ&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg; &lt;&sol;sup&gt;81479 for claims on or after 3&sol;16&sol;2018.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Use PLA 0364U to describe the service for patients with a personal history of cancer. This code has been approved for patients with a history of Mantle Cell Lymphoma.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-gene and panel testing by PCR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding single-gene and panel testing of genes &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A56853 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A57503&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Regarding BCR-ABL1 testing &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A53531 for BCR-ABL1 testing&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.65pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Providers are reminded to refer to the long descriptors of the CPT codes in their CPT book.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;The CPT codes in Group 1 are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met. The 90-day global periods apply.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See L33954 Cataract Extraction LCD and related B&amp;amp;C article for additional coverage indications and diagnoses.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Procedure codes may be subject to National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits or OPPS packaging edits. Refer to NCCI and OPPS requirements prior to billing Medicare.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For services requiring a referring&sol;ordering physician, the name and NPI of the referring&sol;ordering physician must be reported on the claim.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A claim submitted without a valid ICD-10-CM diagnosis code will be returned to the provider as an incomplete claim under &amp;sect;1833(e) of the Social Security Act.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All services&sol;procedures performed on the same day for the same beneficiary by the physician&sol;provider should be billed on the same claim.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Billing for preparatory services&sol;acquisition costs is covered in CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 3, &amp;sect;90.3.1 Allogeneic for Stem Cell Transplantation.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This billing instruction pertains to the Galleri Category B IDE test when performed and billed by GRAIL, LLC (North Carolina). Study information can be found here: &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare&sol;coverage&sol;investigational-device-exemption-ide-studies&sol;approved&quot;&gt;Approved IDE Studies | CMS&lt;&sol;a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare&sol;coverage&sol;ide&sol;approved-ide-studies&sol;1923430381&sol;g220255-nct05673018&quot;&gt;G220255-NCT05673018 | CMS&lt;&sol;a&gt;.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Claims must contain the following information:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Category B IDE number&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Clinical Trial number&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;CPT 81479&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The Z-Code descriptor specific to the &lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Investigational Category B IDE&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt; &lt;&sol;u&gt;Galleri Test&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The appropriate HCPCS Modifier&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The appropriate ICD Diagnosis code&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;A beneficiary may receive up to three &lt;u&gt;Investigational Category B IDE&lt;&sol;u&gt; Galleri tests per lifetime.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Procedure codes may be subject to National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits or Outpatient Prospective Payment System (OPPS) packaging edits. Refer to NCCI and OPPS requirements prior to billing Medicare.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For services requiring a referring&sol;ordering physician, the name and National Provider Indicator (NPI) of the referring&sol;ordering physician must be reported on the claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A claim submitted without a valid ICD-10-CM diagnosis code will be returned to the provider as an incomplete claim under &amp;sect;1833(e) of the Social Security Act.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;All services&sol;procedures performed on the same day for the same beneficiary by the physician&sol;provider should be billed on the same claim.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Billing for preparatory services&sol;acquisition costs is covered in CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 3, &amp;sect;90.3.1 Allogeneic for Stem Cell Transplantation.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The CPT codes are considered medically necessary when the Indications of Coverage are met.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Part A&lt;&sol;u&gt;: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Contractors shall pay claims for SET services containing CPT code 93668 on Types of Bill (TOBs) 13X under OPPS and 85X based on reasonable cost. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Part B&lt;&sol;u&gt;: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Claims for CPT 93668 are limited to be billed in POS 11 only in Part B.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
